WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.780
Phone video and clear sound: shoot, edit and post.

2
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:09.400
This is the video for module 3 of Content Creation with Canva and Phone Tools.

3
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:18.890
You do not need an expensive camera. Most poor phone video comes from shaky hands, bad light, a dirty lens and messy sound.

4
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.770
CapCut is a free editing app that turns separate clips into one clear story.

5
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.460
Short videos reach people who do not follow you yet, if they keep watching.

6
00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:36.530
And viewers forgive slightly soft video, but they leave quickly when the sound is bad.

7
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:48.550
Before you record, clean the lens. A greasy fingerprint is the most common cause of foggy footage. Check storage and battery, and turn on gridlines to keep things level.

8
00:00:48.900 --> 00:01:03.320
Set 1080p at 30 frames per second. It is sharp enough, with smaller files and less data. Switch on airplane mode so a call does not ruin a good take, and shoot vertical for Reels, Shorts and Status.

9
00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:13.850
Light is the biggest free upgrade. Face a window, with daylight falling on your face. Avoid harsh midday sun and mixed yellow and blue lights.

10
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:28.670
Shaky video is tiring to watch. Hold the phone with both hands and elbows tucked in, or rest it on a tripod or a stack of books. Use the main 1x lens. If you need to be closer, walk closer.

11
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:36.750
Tap your subject's face to focus. Press and hold to lock it, so the picture does not pulse lighter and darker.

12
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.850
For example, Nkechi sells zobo in Owerri. She plans a shot list of wide, medium and close-up shots, each 5 to 10 seconds, so she has room to trim.

13
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:58.060
She is filming cooking, so the phone and tripod stay away from hot pots and gas flames. And never film while driving or crossing a road.

14
00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.300
Shot one, wide: her clean counter with the ingredients laid out.

15
00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:08.540
Shot two, close-up: dried hibiscus leaves poured into the pot.

16
00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:13.880
Shot three, medium: her hands adding ginger and pineapple peel.

17
00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:19.230
Shot four, close-up: chilled zobo poured into a branded bottle.

18
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:29.420
Shot five, medium: she holds the bottle, smiles and says, order on WhatsApp. That gives her 34 seconds of steady, bright footage.

19
00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:36.430
In CapCut, tap New project, add your clips in order, and set the format to 9:16.

20
00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:47.810
Drag the white handles to trim slow starts. Nkechi moved her pouring shot to the start as a 2-second hook, and cut her clips into a 25-second Reel.

21
00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:58.830
Add short text and auto captions, because many people watch without sound. Always proofread. CapCut wrote so bow, and she corrected it to zobo.

22
00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:08.760
Add music from CapCut's library at a low volume, like 20%. A popular song from your own phone may be muted or blocked.

23
00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:18.180
Export at 1080p and 30 frames per second. Higher settings only make bigger files that cost more data.

24
00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:32.170
For example, Joy is a hair stylist in Benin City. Her hook is a close-up of finished braids, with the text, Make your braids last 6 weeks. If people leave in the first 3 seconds, improve the hook.

25
00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.940
Her value is three short tips, such as wrapping with a satin scarf at night.

26
00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.840
Her action: book your braids, send a DM.

27
00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:53.070
About 2 to 3 spoken words per second is a natural pace. Her tip format earned more saves than her photo posts, so she now makes one every Wednesday.

28
00:03:54.320 --> 00:04:08.720
The room matters more than the microphone. Soft things absorb echo, so a bedroom with curtains and a wardrobe of clothes works well. Keep the phone about 15 to 20 cm away, and record a 10-second test first.

29
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:19.620
Avoid bare rooms, fans and generator noise. Keep voice notes to customers under one minute, and send the price and delivery details as text too.

30
00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:36.480
To remember. Clean lens, good light, steady phone. Plan wide, medium and close-up shots. Put the best moment first and proofread captions. Hook in 3 seconds, one idea, one action. And record sound in a quiet, soft room.

31
00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:51.150
Your turn. Record a three-shot sequence. Edit it into a 20 to 30 second video. Script and post one short video, and check its insights after 3 days. Then record a 2-minute audio tip.

32
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.440
Continue with the lessons below.
